 hierarchical packing of 16 three-bit codes;\n- direct Packed20x3 output packing without a full-capacity temporary entry\n  array or a second packing pass.\n\nThe 2026-09-01 refactor also removed the legacy TP3/TilePalette kernels,\nGPU encoders, duplicate decode entry points, compatibility aliases, unused\ndecode metadata, and three research-only benchmark scripts. Native sources and\nthe extension are now named `chunk_delta3.*` / `chunk_delta3_ext`. KV codec\nsize and full-block capabilities live in the lightweight `kv_codec_spec.py`\nregistry, shared by tiered-serve and the vLLM planners without importing CUDA\ncompressor modules. Known codec allocation/copy/decode failures now fail fast;\nthe production KV decode path requires the published active-set plan and\n`cudaMemcpyBatchAsync` support.\n\nThe consolidated snapshot additionally contains:\n\n- host-native CD3 weight encoding with 64-row stripe parallelism;\n- adaptive OpenMP team sizing for a single KV compression worker;\n- batched NumPy KV slot allocation instead of a per-block Python loop;\n- production fused-MM crossover calibration through N=128 on GH200.\n- 128-thread standalone CD3 decode, with two logical chunks per thread;\n- two half-width live output accumulators with the same two 128-bit stores,\n  reducing standalone decode latency without changing the format;\n- 2-D `(tile, block)` KV decode launch geometry;\n- direct-to-cache indexed KV decode with no raw-BF16 intermediate copy;\n- selected-run KV staging for partial restores below the slot high-water mark.\n- one aligned slot-major CD3 blob and row-stride-aware CPU/GPU kernels;\n- one `cudaMemcpyBatchAsync` submission for all K/V staging runs;\n- cached block/slot device metadata and one native K/V decode dispatch.\n- active-set identity/content caching with generation-safe invalidation;\n- a dense steady-state decode plan that skips filtering, sorting and run scans.\n- once-per-forward active-set publication instead of repeated per-layer NumPy\n  comparisons;\n- explicit-stream native paired decode dispatch;\n- a two-slot compressed-blob HBM ring that overlaps layer L+1 H2D with layer L\n  decode for N>=256, while preserving the cheaper one-stream path below it;\n- serving-suite codec selection through `--codecs p4flat,cd3`, including\n  codec-specific weight/KV arguments, configs, result labels and manifests;\n- a fully CPU P4Flat weight post-process (blocked relayout and subtile codec),\n  so CPU weight encoding no longer launches CUDA encode kernels;\n- a frozen-split weight benchmark that separately reports H2D, resident GPU\n  decode, and their combined latency.\n- projection-specific fused-N calibration overrides, with a uniform override\n  retained for compatibility;\n- exact-length CD3 frozen-split staging views, so standalone fallback accepts\n  variable-sized Packed20x3 exception streams;\n- startup route reporting that reflects projection-specific overrides.\n- a GH200/Llama-70B prefill weight-stream cutoff of N=1856: compressed\n  standalone decode below the cutoff and raw BF16 transfer at or above it;\n- an AST-level regression test that pins the calibrated CD3 cutoff.\n\n## Validation\n\n- The old CD3 patch's complete path set is contained in this patch.\n- Applied cleanly after startup prerequisites on source HEAD.\n- All 33 restored tiered-serve files matched the selected live files\n  byte-for-byte.\n- `git diff --check`, Python byte compilation, and shell syntax checks passed.\n- The consolidated patch applied after both startup prerequisites in a clean\n  worktree and all 32 restored files matched the live files byte-for-byte.\n- The vLLM integration patch reverse-checks against the validated live tree.\n- 33 CD3, prefill weight-stream, and KV-prefill policy tests passed.\n- The renamed `chunk_delta3_ext` built and imported successfully.\n- Synthetic CPU weight encode/GPU decode, CPU KV encode, and KV H2D+decode\n  smoke benchmarks were bit-exact.\n- Offline suite smoke (`cao-cd3-fused-kvcomp`, batch 1, input 8, output 2)\n  completed successfully and restored a clean GPU/hugepage boundary.\n- Online suite smoke (`cd3`, `kvcomp`, chunk 64, two requests) completed with\n  2/2 successful requests, 4,455 input tokens, 118 output tokens, and a clean\n  GPU/hugepage boundary. The serving suite now exposes `--smoke`; normal suite\n  defaults remain unchanged.\n- The offline suite now includes a non-fused `cao-cd3` cell and a\n  `--breakdown` switch that forwards `--time-breakdown` to every selected\n  method. A three-method/five-batch dry-run verified the non-fused, fused, and\n  fused+KV-compression command separation.\n- Actual Llama-3.1-70B weight round-trip: qkv/o/gateup/down all bit-exact.\n- Layer-40 CD3 CPU weight encode median total: 130.7 ms, versus P4Flat CPU\n  1951.9 ms (about 14.9x faster); compression ratio about 1.368x versus 1.326x.\n- GH200 CPU KV encode median with one serving worker, K+V: N=8 0.16 ms;\n  N=64 0.27 ms; N=128 0.37 ms; N=256 0.47 ms; N=1024 0.99 ms;\n  N=2048 2.02 ms. All cases were bit-exact.\n- Full serving initialization installed all 320 fused Linear overrides and\n  completed all 320 CPU-compressed weight cells.\n- Layer-40 standalone weight decode median gained another 1.4% in aggregate\n  from half-width live output accumulation (all four groups bit-exact).\n- Resident production KV decode improved 1.69x--2.04x for N=8/64/256 by\n  writing directly to the final cache. Partial H2D restore at high-water=1024\n  improved 16% for N=64 and 12% for N=256.\n- Final current-stride standalone K+V H2D+decode medians for CD3 are\n  0.043/0.041/0.079/0.223 ms at N=8/64/256/1024 versus P4Flat\n  0.062/0.065/0.092/0.247 ms, making CD3 30.6/36.0/13.8/9.8% faster.\n- A 16-layer CD3 pipeline gains 30.3% at N=256 and 25.8% at N=1024 from\n  H2D/decode overlap; all cases remained bit-exact.\n- CPU-encoded production KV H2D+decode steady-state median on GH200 is\n  0.065/0.065/0.102/0.251 ms for N=8/64/256/1024. P4Flat under the same\n  split-measurement run is 0.063/0.070/0.107/0.302 ms. CD3 resident decode is\n  0.028/0.029/0.036/0.065 ms versus P4Flat 0.046/0.047/0.049/0.082 ms; CD3\n  H2D is 0.016/0.026/0.056/0.173 ms versus 0.030/0.042/0.081/0.232 ms.\n  The pre-blob CD3 values were\n  0.247/0.291/0.374/0.762 ms; all cases were bit-exact. This historical P4Flat\n  comparison used its raw-safe 32,768-byte blob stride. Current P4Flat defaults\n  to a 25,600-byte tight stride, so these P4Flat values must not be used as the\n  final current-codec comparison.\n- Layer-40 frozen-split weight medians on GH200 (qkv/o/gateup/down summed):\n  CD3 H2D 1.200 ms, resident decode 0.923 ms, H2D+decode 2.127 ms; P4Flat\n  H2D 1.353 ms, resident decode 0.906 ms, H2D+decode 2.232 ms. CD3 therefore\n  transfers 11.3% faster and finishes the production pair 4.7% faster while\n  its isolated decode is 1.9% slower. All four weights were bit-exact.\n- Rejected experiments are not present: warp-owner exception pre-application\n  was about 2.3x slower, pairwise 3xU32 code loading was neutral/regressive,\n  64-thread or register-forced 10-CTA kernels were 7--12% slower, and a\n  separate standalone exception kernel was 50.7% slower than integrated patch.\n- Fused route calibration with concurrent H2D found all four projections faster\n  for every tested N=65..128. At N=129 the Npad=192 transition makes fused\n  about 1.6--1.7x slower, so the production cutoff is exactly 128.\n- An all-80-layer QKV sweep found fused wins on 79/80 layers and saves\n  0.508/0.595/1.211 ms in aggregate at N=80/96/128. The exception-heavy layer\n  0 is the sole loser. End-to-end TPOT P50 for all-fused versus QKV-standalone\n  was 171.90/188.40/219.26 versus 172.20/187.96/219.30 ms at batch\n  80/96/128, confirming a tie at engine level and favoring all-fused because it\n  avoids dense-weight HBM writes.\n- End-to-end forced-route prefill sweeps placed the standalone/raw crossover\n  between N=1824 and N=1856. At N=1824 standalone led by 18.630 ms; at N=1856\n  raw led by 20.405 ms, and raw remained ahead through N=3072. An unforced run\n  confirmed standalone routing at N=1792/1824 and raw routing at N=1856/1888.\n  The full report and source logs are stored under\n  `/lambda/nfs/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-20260901-route/`.\n- Final whole-engine Llama-70B TPOT median is 114.51 ms versus P4Flat\n  124.66 ms at batch 64 (8.14% faster), and 166.64 versus 180.59 ms at batch\n  128 (7.72% faster). Both methods used CPU weight/KV encode and production\n  GPU decode/fused routing.\n+  sampler: null\n+frozen_blocks:\n+  \"model.layers.*.input_layernorm\": null\n+  \"model.layers.*.self_attn.rotary_emb\": null\n+  \"model.layers.*.post_attention_layernorm\": null\n+  model.norm: null\n+  lm_head: null\n+  logits_processor: null\n+  sampler: null\n+\n+ats_blocks:\n+  model.embed_tokens: null\n+\n+# frozen_split: sign_mantissa on HBM (~59 GB), rest on LPDDR (~41 GB)\n+# Designed for GH200 (96 GB HBM + LPDDR5)\n+layer_residency:\n+  default:\n+    qkv: {mode: offload_compressed, compressor: chunk_delta3}\n+    o: {mode: offload_compressed, compressor: chunk_delta3}\n+    gate_up: {mode: offload_compressed, compressor: chunk_delta3}\n+    down: {mode: offload_compressed, compressor: chunk_delta3}\n+  frozen:\n+    qkv:\n+      mode: frozen_split\n+      compressor: chunk_delta3\n+      layers: all\n+    o:\n+      mode: frozen_split\n+      compressor: chunk_delta3\n+      layers: all\n+    gate_up:\n+      mode: frozen_split\n+      compressor: chunk_delta3\n+      layers: all\n+    down:\n+      mode: frozen_split\n+      compressor: chunk_delta3\n+      layers: all\ndiff --git a/tiered_serve/tensor_compressor.py b/tiered_serve/tensor_compressor.py\nindex 0bc765861fbc4f8d6938298e6c560b703c7ef599..568ec90899dafa6b0c251e13e6bd59d62d00e2ba 100644\n--- a/tiered_serve/tensor_compressor.py\n+++ b/tiered_serve/tensor_compressor.py\n@@ -67,6 +67,11 @@ from tiered_serve.compression.core.p4flat import (  # noqa: F401\n     CompressedP4FlatTensor,\n     P4FlatCompressor,\n )\n+from tiered_serve.compression.core.chunk_delta3 import (  # noqa: F401\n+    _HAS_CHUNK_DELTA3,\n+    CompressedChunkDelta3Tensor,\n+    ChunkDelta3Compressor,\n+)\n from tiered_serve.compression.core.zipserv_ot import (  # noqa: F401\n     _HAS_ZSV_OT,\n     CompressedZipServOTTensor,\ndiff --git a/tiered_serve/torch_hooks.py b/tiered_serve/torch_hooks.py\nindex c88aeeb1f5042e347f7699b638b8895b97abb041..9413ea53289736090d7e11c906371158948f941d 100644\n--- a/tiered_serve/torch_hooks.py\n+++ b/tiered_serve/torch_hooks.py\n@@ -339,10 +339,20 @@ def before_model_forward(self, input):\n         )\n \n     if DualMemoryLoader.use_kv_comp:\n+        # Publish the canonical active set once per forward.  CD3 uses the\n+        # held list identity plus a content version to skip an O(N) active-set\n+        # comparison in every layer; codecs without this optional hook retain\n+        # their existing path unchanged.\n+        kc = getattr(dm_loader, \"kv_compressor\", None)\n+        prepare_active = getattr(kc, \"prepare_active_set\", None)\n+        if prepare_active is not None:\n+            prepare_active(\n+                dm_loader.active_kv_buffer_ids,\n+                dm_loader.np_active_kv_buffer_ids,\n+            )\n         # Publish the per-step occupancy map for the P4Flat KV compressor\n         # (only when occupancy mode is enabled).  Replaced (not mutated) each\n         # step so in-flight compress workers keep their own step's snapshot.\n-        kc = getattr(dm_loader, \"kv_compressor\", None)\n         if kc is not None and getattr(kc, \"_occupancy_enabled\", False):\n             bs = (DualMemoryLoader.primary_k_caches[0].shape[1]\n                   if hasattr(DualMemoryLoader, \"primary_k_caches\")\n271d02de4ed6c9a8c07cd151e04ab4b419763e0e4dadb4b997c8457d2ce0ee1e  cd3_current.patch\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06186-6325-79b3-9454-03c11387a0a9",